WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:06.360
With more choices than ever, trying to choose
what to watch can be exciting and overwhelming

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:07.620
at the same time.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:12.900
If you need help choosing which prestige drama
or quirky comedy to pick up next, we've collected

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.789
the very best new television options of the
year.

00:00:16.789 --> 00:00:21.679
Adapting one of Stephen King's many acclaimed
works is pretty much always a recipe for success,

00:00:21.679 --> 00:00:23.980
whether it's on the big or small screen.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.740
HBO's The Outsider is no exception.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:31.339
One of King's most recent works — the novel
was published in 2018 — tells the story

00:00:31.339 --> 00:00:36.370
of Oklahoma Detective Ralph Anderson, who
arrests Terry Maitland , a respected citizen

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:41.190
who coaches Little League, for the brutal
assault and murder of an 11-year-old boy.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:46.100
Though there's physical evidence tying Maitland
to the crime, he still has an alibi, and it's

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:51.430
Anderson's responsibility to break Maitland,
even as the town stirs itself into a fervor

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:53.070
in the background.

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:57.430
Starring Ben Mendelsohn and Jason Bateman
and boasting a stellar supporting cast that

00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:02.880
includes Julianne Nicholson, Cynthia Erivo
, Mare Winningham , and Bill Camp, The Outsider

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:08.640
was a surefire win thanks to its excellent
source material and pitch-perfect performances,

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.130
and critics agreed.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:15.130
The series earned rave reviews, particularly
singling out Erivo for her scene-stealing

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:16.479
supporting turn.

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:20.731
There are plenty of crime dramas on television
these days, but The Outsider is a standout.

00:01:22.549 --> 00:01:27.020
Ever since her breakout year in 2018, where
she stole supporting scenes in movies like

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:32.340
Ocean's 8 and Crazy Rich Asians, Awkwafina
has become a huge Hollywood star.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:37.700
Though she recently won acclaim for her dramatic
turn in 2019's The Farewell, she's still primarily

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.740
a comedic actor, which she displays to excellent
effect in Comedy Central's Awkwafina Is Nora

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.020
from Queens.

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:49.979
Developed and written by Awkwafina herself,
the show is based on the actress' true life,

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:54.540
her close relationship with her Chinese family
and her struggles as she tries to make it

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:55.980
in New York City.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:02:01.439
Critics loved Nora from Queens just as much
as they've loved Awkwafina's other performances;

00:02:01.439 --> 00:02:05.619
despite tackling the familiar territory of
chronicling a 20-something woman's struggles

00:02:05.619 --> 00:02:11.380
in New York, Awkwafina's performance and the
show itself both earned overwhelming praise.

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:16.601
If you want to learn more about her real past
and love a good coming-of-age story, Awkwafina

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:19.510
Is Nora from Queens is definitely for you.

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:25.430
A Netflix adaptation of a Harlan Coben novel,
The Stranger comes by way of the U.K., packed

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:29.360
with British actors to create yet another
great crime drama.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:34.100
The series stars Richard Armitage as Adam
Price, who is married with two sons.

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:39.020
His life is turned upside down one day when
a mysterious woman known only as the Stranger

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:42.520
appears and tells him a secret about his wife,
Corinne.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:47.450
When Corinne disappears during the aftermath,
Adam must track down his wife, while the Stranger

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:52.770
continues moving about town to blackmail and
extort anybody with a secret they'd rather

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:53.770
keep quiet.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:55.200
"One more thing.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:03:01.150
If I were you, I'd run DNA checks on your
two boys."

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:05.031
Thanks to its excellent supporting cast and
the gripping mystery of the Stranger, who

00:03:05.031 --> 00:03:11.000
reveals herself more and more throughout eight
episodes, the series earned raves from critics,

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.310
who praised its careful plotting and exciting
tension.

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:18.860
Whether you're a fan of Coben's work or new
to his stories, The Stranger is absolutely

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:19.870
worth a watch.

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:26.040
Adapted from Philip Roth's famous and acclaimed
novel, the HBO miniseries The Plot Against

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:30.850
America envisions a frightening alternate
history that bears some unsettling resemblance

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:32.690
to the world we live in today.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:37.540
In this different reality, Charles Lindbergh,
the famous aviator who closely aligned himself

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:42.530
with fascist efforts and the Nazi movement
during World War II, becomes President of

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:46.720
the United States and immediately targets
the American Jewish population.

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:51.650
As anti-Semitism spreads across the country,
one Jewish family in Newark must navigate

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:54.080
their new reality and try to survive.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:04:00.500
With an outstanding cast that includes Winona
Ryder, Zoe Kazan , John Turturro, David Krumholtz

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:05.490
and more, The Plot Against America earned
raves from critics for its handsomely realized

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:09.430
revisionism, though they did note that it
can be a difficult watch for some viewers

00:04:09.430 --> 00:04:13.010
due to its undeniable relevance in such a
different time.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:17.850
The Plot Against America might be tough at
times, but it's also already earned its place

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:20.709
as one of the most important series of the
year.

00:04:21.709 --> 00:04:26.460
Ever since Big Little Lies took television
by storm in 2017, viewers have clamored for

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:32.150
similar stories set in seemingly tranquil,
wealthy suburban areas with drama simmering

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.310
just underneath the surface.

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:39.880
Little Fires Everywhere, a Hulu original based
on the novel by Celeste Ng , fits that bill

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:40.880
perfectly.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:45.760
The two shows even share a major cast member
in common, as Reese Witherspoon heads up both

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:46.760
series.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:51.200
In Little Fires Everywhere, she plays Elena
Richardson, a 1990s housewife living in Shaker

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:56.520
Heights, Ohio who finds herself at odds with
Mia Warren, played by Kerry Washington, who

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:00.710
stirs up trouble among the Richardson family
and in the neighborhood.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:04.890
Despite the inevitable comparisons to Big
Little Lies, Little Fires Everywhere is a

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:06.980
standout in its own right.

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:12.750
Its first season has had critics raving, particularly
about Witherspoon and Washington's performances.

00:05:12.750 --> 00:05:16.970
Shaker Heights might not seem like the world's
most exciting locale, but if Little Fires

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:21.390
Everywhere is to be believed, it's much more
dramatic than anyone ever imagined.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:26.960
Between The Office and The Mindy Project,
Mindy Kaling has had an amazing career on

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:31.500
the small screen, and Never Have I Ever is
the latest feather in her cap.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:36.280
The semi-autobiographical story of a young
first-generation Indian girl growing up in

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:41.020
California, Never Have I Ever marks the debut
of star Maitreyi Ramakrishnan , who plays

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:45.700
Devi , a 15-year-old with big dreams who's
about to start her sophomore year of high

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:46.700
school.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:51.960
From there, she navigates life, love, and
loss; shortly before the series begins, Devi

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:57.270
loses her father unexpectedly, temporarily
leaving her without the use of her legs.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:06:01.780
Mixing a romantic comedy about young love
and high school trysts with a pitch-perfect

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:07.430
coming-of-age story makes Never Have I Ever
an instant classic for audiences of all ages,

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.200
for a number of reasons.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:13.740
As co-creator Lang Fisher said in an interview
with Buzzfeed, the show is driven by a passion

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:14.740
for representation.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:19.500
Kaling would watch teen shows and not see
herself represented, driving her to want to

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.830
offer that to this generation.

00:06:21.830 --> 00:06:26.340
There's no question that Kaling achieved her
goal, and with another hit under her belt,

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:30.850
this creator has cemented herself as one of
television's most important voices.

00:06:30.850 --> 00:06:33.900
"I knew it was you.

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:36.960
I miss you so much.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:41.240
You're here to cheer me up, right?"

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:47.180
Unorthodox is adapted from Deborah Feldman's
2012 memoir Unorthodox: The Scandalous Rejection

00:06:47.180 --> 00:06:48.700
of My Hasidic Roots.

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:53.480
It tells the daring story of one girl's escape
from a restrictive, conservative community

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.590
and made waves when it premiered in early
2020.

00:06:56.590 --> 00:07:02.120
The miniseries stars Shira Haas as Esty , a
19-year-old woman in the Orthodox Jewish faith

00:07:02.120 --> 00:07:04.919
who is suffering through an arranged marriage.

00:07:04.919 --> 00:07:09.680
After escaping Williamsburg, Brooklyn, Esty
makes her way to Berlin to find her long-lost

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.889
mother and establish a new life.

00:07:11.889 --> 00:07:17.270
However, her husband comes looking for her
after he finds out some life-changing news:

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.700
Esty is pregnant.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:24.450
Upon its release, critics and audiences alike
loved Unorthodox and widely praised Haas'

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:25.560
central performance.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:30.680
Though the story is extraordinarily specific,
most viewers can relate to Esty's desire to

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:35.870
live in a different world, making Unorthodox
a surprisingly universal story despite its

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:36.870
tight focus.

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:42.590
Based on the popular novel of the same name
by Irish writer Sally Rooney, Hulu's original

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:47.930
series Normal People tells the story of Marianne
Sheridan and Connell Waldron, two teenagers

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:51.590
whose love story spans years and social standings.

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:56.150
When the two meet in secondary school on the
coast of Ireland, popular student athlete

00:07:56.150 --> 00:08:01.540
Connell immediately connects with Marianne,
a shy, bookish oddball, and their relationship

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:05.190
intensifies away from the judgmental eyes
of their peers.

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:10.270
However, when they both go to Trinity College,
their roles reverse, and Marianne's intelligence

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:14.290
is prized over Connell's brawn, creating an
imbalance.

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:18.800
Hulu's series has proven just as successful
as Rooney's acclaimed novel, earning raves

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:23.580
from critics for its slow, sensitive, and
thoughtful portrayal of a young couple throughout

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:24.710
the years.

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:29.610
Despite its often dark outlook on love and
relationships, Normal People is a relatable,

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:34.750
gripping story about young love and emotional
hurdles, and with Daisy Edgar-Jones and Paul

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:40.340
Mescal delivering excellent starring performances,
the story becomes even more powerful.

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:45.010
Afterlife comedies are all the rage these
days, and in the wake of The Good Place's

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:48.440
finale, fans can turn to the Amazon Prime
series Upload.

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:55.170
Set in 2033, the show follows Nathan Brown,
who dies young and is "uploaded" to a pre-programmed

00:08:55.170 --> 00:09:00.839
luxury heaven called Lake View by a company
called Horizen thanks to his wealthy girlfriend.

00:09:00.839 --> 00:09:06.130
Though Nathan is initially dismayed and dissatisfied
by the neighborhood, he eventually comes around

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:11.360
thanks to his assigned customer service representative,
or "Angel," who is actually a living human

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:13.760
named Nora who works for Horizen.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:18.640
However, as Nathan and Nora spend more time
together, they start developing unexpected

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:23.200
feelings for one another, and Nora starts
looking into Nathan's untimely death.

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:28.350
Created by Greg Daniels of The Office and
Parks and Recreation, Upload's wry humor and

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:33.330
excellent central performances won over critics
and audiences alike, and the show has already

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:35.270
been renewed for a second season.

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:39.460
If you're looking for a replacement for The
Good Place, Upload will definitely keep you

00:09:39.460 --> 00:09:40.460
entertained.

00:09:40.460 --> 00:09:44.050
"Well, I'm not worried about scaring you off
now.

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:46.190
Talk later babe, k?"

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:53.110
The premise of Zoey's Extraordinary Playlist
might sound pretty crazy, but thanks to grounding

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:59.150
central performances and a big heart, creator
Austin Winberg's series pulls things off perfectly.

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:04.560
Led by Jane Levy as Zoey, the show tells the
story of a serious, often stern computer programmer

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:10.040
in San Francisco who undergoes an MRI during
an earthquake and emerges from the machine

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:12.170
with a surprising new power.

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:17.490
After her brain scan, Zoey can suddenly hear
people singing when nobody else can, and quickly

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:22.200
figures out that these songs are their heart
songs, meaning that they express the person's

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:24.589
innermost hopes, desires, and feelings.

00:10:24.589 --> 00:10:26.370
"I'm just very, very confused.

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:30.640
You said that I was getting a glimpse into
other peoples' heads."

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:34.610
As Zoey tries to manage her new ability with
the help of her musically talented friend

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:40.050
and neighbor Mo, she must also navigate a
love triangle between an attractive new co-worker

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:44.920
and her best friend, as well as help care
for her ailing father, who suffers from a

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:48.870
terminal illness that causes his body to deteriorate.

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:53.290
Despite the objectively out-there premise,
Zoey's Extraordinarily Playlist balances an

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:59.089
imaginary power with very real problems perfectly,
and Levy, with her lived-in performance and

00:10:59.089 --> 00:11:02.470
effortless charm, keeps the show from veering
into absurdity.

00:11:03.930 --> 00:11:08.420
New takes on familiar characters are a dime
a dozen, but in their latest revival of one

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:13.570
of pop culture's most famous lawyers, HBO
has yet another critical darling on their

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:15.040
hands with Perry Mason.

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:21.500
An origin story set in the 1930s, this new
series casts Matthew Rhys as Perry Mason just

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:24.080
as he begins his career as a defense lawyer.

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:28.470
Still struggling with his memories of World
War I and going through a divorce, Perry,

00:11:28.470 --> 00:11:33.680
now in Los Angeles, is brought onto a headline-making
case concerning the kidnapping of a young

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:36.160
child, changing his life forever.

00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:41.580
With backing from HBO and a cast that includes
beloved stars like Tatiana Maslany , John

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:46.490
Lithgow, and Shea Whigham , there's no surprise
that critics fell in love during its inaugural

00:11:46.490 --> 00:11:50.720
season, praising it as stylish and compelling
with an excellent cast.

00:11:50.720 --> 00:11:55.310
Perry Mason is a classic character, and with
this new version of his story and Rhys in

00:11:55.310 --> 00:11:59.880
the lead, new generations will surely continue
to discover his stories.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:05.540
Adapting a popular movie for television isn't
always the best idea, but in the spring of

00:12:05.540 --> 00:12:10.420
2020, Hulu proved nonbelievers wrong with
their new version of High Fidelity, 20 years

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:12.630
after the original film hit theaters.

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:18.430
However, the new version comes with a twist:
John Cusack's Rob, a record store owner looking

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:24.470
for love in all the wrong places, is replaced
by Zoë Kravitz as a new character, who's

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:28.410
also named Rob and owns a cool record shop
in Brooklyn.

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:33.020
"Okay, so, here's how not to plan a career."

00:12:33.020 --> 00:12:38.149
Navigating her love life amidst several exes,
Kravitz's Rob is rough around the edges, but

00:12:38.149 --> 00:12:43.060
thanks in large part to Kravitz's pitch-perfect
performance as she speaks directly to the

00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:47.310
camera, the show immediately succeeds in getting
you to root for her.

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:52.110
Critics almost universally adored this new
take on Cusack's classic film, based on the

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:57.270
original novel by Nick Hornby . Kravitz's
performance anchors the entire show, and she

00:12:57.270 --> 00:13:02.589
is more than up to the task of putting forth
the charming, vulnerable and powerful performance

00:13:02.589 --> 00:13:04.090
the series needs.

00:13:04.090 --> 00:13:09.110
Unfortunately, Hulu canceled the series after
its debut season, leaving fans with just ten

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:11.600
episodes of this warm, funny show.

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:15.209
That said, those ten episodes are absolutely
worth a watch.

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:21.080
Historical dramas can easily become a bit
dry and boring, but in the case of Hulu's

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:26.089
The Great, facts matter a lot less than camp,
high drama and glamour.

00:13:26.089 --> 00:13:30.920
Developed by Tony McNamara, who earned fame
and acclaim in 2018 for his screenplay for

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:36.140
The Favourite, The Great is relatively similar
to McNamara's big screen venture, using modern

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:41.050
language and other anachronisms to boost the
entertainment value while still telling a

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:42.540
somewhat true story.

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:47.860
This time, McNamara put his focus on Catherine
the Great in the years before she became Empress

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:52.780
of Russia, chronicling her difficult marriage
to the hapless lout Peter the third.

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:57.140
As Catherine adjusts to her new life in Russia,
she begins to plot a coup , and it's hardly

00:13:57.140 --> 00:14:02.850
a spoiler alert to say that as the series
continues, she's increasingly sure to succeed.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:08.120
Upon its release, critics agreed that The
Great was, well, great, thanks to McNamara's

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:13.310
wicked sense of humor and perfect performances
from Elle Fanning and Nicholas Hoult in the

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:14.330
lead roles.

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:18.800
Catherine the Great has long been regarded
as one of Russia's most important leaders,

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:22.300
so it's fitting that her modern adaptation
is so excellent.

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:28.570
Based on Michelle McNamara's acclaimed book,
HBO struck gold with the innovative I'll Be

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:33.220
Gone in the Dark, which stands alone as one
of the most personal and intimate true crime

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.209
shows in recent memory.

00:14:35.209 --> 00:14:41.110
McNamara, who tragically passed away at the
age of 46 in 2016, spent years hunting the

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:45.630
true identity of a serial killer known as
the Golden State Killer, and the series takes

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:50.621
a creative approach to both her story and
the legend of the Golden State Killer, chronicling

00:14:50.621 --> 00:14:54.480
the journey required for her to write the
book in the first place.

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:59.810
With voiceovers from Amy Ryan, plenty of assistance
from McNamara's bereft husband — comedian

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:05.250
Patton Oswalt, who provided essential information
— and a careful hand from its showrunners,

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:10.310
I'll Be Gone in the Dark doesn't glorify the
killer, but looks at the lives he impacted.

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:15.430
Critics loved the personal focus on McNamara's
life and the Golden State Killer's victims.

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:20.120
Ultimately, McNamara's efforts helped catch
the serial killer after her death; now, I'll

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:24.320
Be Gone in the Dark is yet another piece of
her incredible legacy.

00:15:25.410 --> 00:15:30.110
Anti-heroes are nothing new, but anti-heroines
are becoming more common, and the difficult

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:34.899
leading lady of Mrs. America arrived on the
small screen at just the right time.

00:15:34.899 --> 00:15:41.829
A joint effort between Hulu and FX, the 1970s-set
miniseries Mrs. America tells the story of

00:15:41.829 --> 00:15:47.310
the battle over the Equal Rights Amendment,
profiling both its champions and its opponents.

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:52.390
The cast is peppered with some serious heavyweight
performers playing real-life historical and

00:15:52.390 --> 00:15:53.829
political figures.

00:15:53.829 --> 00:15:59.180
With Cate Blanchett as anti-feminist Phyllis
Schlafly , Rose Byrne as Gloria Steinem, Margo

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:05.829
Martindale as Bella Abzug , Tracey Ullman
as Betty Freidan , and Uzo Aduba as groundbreaking

00:16:05.829 --> 00:16:10.899
Black female Presidential candidate Shirley
Chisholm , Mrs. America shows both sides of

00:16:10.899 --> 00:16:16.420
the debate over equal rights for women, casting
Schlafly in a particularly unflattering light.

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:21.610
With this powerhouse cast, it's no surprise
that Mrs. America succeeded right out of the

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:26.060
gate, with critics loving the ensemble cast
and the way they brought to life the vast

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:28.990
array of different personalities in the series.

00:16:28.990 --> 00:16:33.440
Chronicling this important period of history
is quite an undertaking, but Mrs. America

00:16:33.440 --> 00:16:34.899
pulls it off with distinction.

00:16:34.899 --> 00:16:39.240
"We do not want housewives thinking we are
against them."

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:41.160
"We are against them."

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:42.589
"Revolutions are messy.

00:16:42.589 --> 00:16:44.510
People get left behind."

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:50.900
Michael Jordan is one of the world's most
legendary athletes, but it took until 2020

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:55.390
for a definitive documentary series about
one of his biggest victories to hit the small

00:16:55.390 --> 00:16:56.390
screen.

00:16:56.390 --> 00:17:01.230
An original Netflix miniseries produced with
ESPN, The Last Dance tells the story of Jordan's

00:17:01.230 --> 00:17:07.119
final season with the Chicago Bulls and their
goal to win their sixth NBA title within eight

00:17:07.119 --> 00:17:11.669
years, despite mounting pressure from the
entire world resting on Jordan's towering

00:17:11.669 --> 00:17:12.669
shoulders.

00:17:12.669 --> 00:17:17.360
Combining archive footage with recent interviews,
The Last Dance serves as a comprehensive look

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:22.370
at one of basketball's greatest seasons, and
critics lauded the series, saying that the

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:27.289
show was a compelling look at one of the greatest
athletes of all time, and helped to further

00:17:27.289 --> 00:17:30.000
cement Jordan as a true living legend.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.779
Even if you're not a sports fan, you'll still
be fascinated by The Last Dance.

00:17:35.009 --> 00:17:39.789
You might know actor and creator Mikaela Coel
from shows like Black Mirror and Chewing Gum,

00:17:39.789 --> 00:17:45.210
but you've never seen her as raw, creative
or exposed as she is in HBO's I May Destroy

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:46.210
You.

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:50.669
Throughout this heartbreaking series, viewers
follow Coel as Arabella, a millennial writer

00:17:50.669 --> 00:17:55.470
who wakes up after a wild night out with a
few fleeting memories of being assaulted.

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:59.889
Initially, Arabella is on a simple mission
to find out what happened to her, but as the

00:17:59.889 --> 00:18:05.260
series evolves, so does the narrative, creating
a complicated, dark and intense story of the

00:18:05.260 --> 00:18:10.119
realities of assault and the culture surrounding
it, the difficulties of social media and what

00:18:10.119 --> 00:18:12.119
it means to seek revenge.

00:18:12.119 --> 00:18:15.009
"Are you OK?

00:18:15.009 --> 00:18:18.859
There is… blood dripping."

00:18:18.859 --> 00:18:23.539
As the series continued, Coel was hailed as
the next great creative mind on television,

00:18:23.539 --> 00:18:28.299
and thanks to a devastatingly perfect ending,
I May Destroy You has earned its spot in the

00:18:28.299 --> 00:18:30.220
television hall of fame.

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:34.999
Critics flocked to praise the show, saying
that it is both brave and thoughtful, utilizing

00:18:34.999 --> 00:18:40.480
stellar writing, dark humor and Coel's many
talents to tell a remarkable tale of trauma

00:18:40.480 --> 00:18:41.889
and how we cope with it.

00:18:41.889 --> 00:18:46.990
I May Destroy You might destroy you, but you
won't regret spending time in Coel's world.

